From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emaki contributors <emaki@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 04:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] tty: exit with status 3 when the primary renderer is missing

On a TTY, niri draws every output with the primary GPU's renderer. When that
renderer cannot be created (software EGL is rejected: llvmpipe on simpledrm,
a VM without 3D acceleration, Hyper-V; or the driver fails), Tty::init only
logs a warning and niri keeps running with no output and no way to notice:
the screen keeps the boot log or stays black for good.

Tty::init now reports whether the primary renderer exists after the device
loop (the dmabuf global is created together with it). When it does not, the
primary GPU was in the device list taken at start (a primary GPU that
registered later is left to its udev "added" event, as in stock niri), and
the session was active at start, State::new returns NoPrimaryRenderer, main
logs "no primary GPU renderer (software EGL rejected or driver failed)",
drops the event loop and exits with status 3. The seat session lives in the
loop's session notifier, so dropping the loop closes the seat: logind and
seatd put the VT back in text mode before they answer, and the text failure
screen printed after the exit is visible. A working secondary GPU does not change this: nothing can be drawn without
the primary renderer. Exit status 3 is the contract emaki-greeter-compositor
relies on to show its text failure screen; other errors keep their behaviour.
Starting on an inactive session is unchanged.

Generated with git diff against the emaki-wallpaper branch; no commit or index mutation.
---
diff --git a/src/backend/mod.rs b/src/backend/mod.rs
index 49fbc6b0..c2442cb1 100644
--- a/src/backend/mod.rs
+++ b/src/backend/mod.rs
@@ -20,6 +20,25 @@ pub use winit::Winit;
 pub mod headless;
